    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1250 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Divination, a major component of folk religion, has developed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> by 1250–1150 BCE</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1000 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The Yijing and the Eight Trigrams are well established</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">531</span><span class="rf-text">A cult of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganesha">Ganesha</a>, the Elephant-Head God, is attested, as influences from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a> arrive with the spread of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">960–1279</span><span class="rf-text">Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a> folk practices blend with Buddhist, Confucian and Taoist teachings into the popular religion that lasts to the present</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1898</span><span class="rf-text">Kang Youwei persuades the emperor to order temples that perform no state sacrifices turned into schools; the confiscations are soon reversed</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1928</span><span class="rf-text">The Nationalist government’s “Standards for retaining or abolishing gods and shrines” try to abolish the cults of all gods but great heroes and sages</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1966–1976</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultural-revolution">Cultural Revolution</a> makes the most serious and last systematic effort to destroy the ancient Chinese religion</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1978</span><span class="rf-text">After the adoption of the new constitution the religion revives rapidly, with millions of temples rebuilt or built from scratch</span></li></ol>
    </section>

